Tark: no Translate unless the user brings a server (spec 5.2). The app-menu
item shows only with ungoogled-chromium's --translate-script-url, like its
context-menu item; the Languages page loses its Google Translate card; Live
Translate, which sends captions to Google, is off.

On the desktop (Mac, Windows, Linux), page-translate/desktop-ui.patch
turns this around: Translate is Tark's own translator, shown while
Settings › Languages › Page translation is on (that switch takes the card's
place) and --translate-script-url is ignored. It does so on top of this
patch, which stays as it is for Android (whose Translate surfaces are its
own patches).

